# VIGIL SaaS money-IN drain — config for vigil-billing-drain.service   (MONEY path)
# Copy to ~/.config/vigil/billing-drain.env with mode 0600 (`install -m 600 …`) and fill in. NEVER commit the
# filled-in file: it holds the webhook verif-hash secret and the payment-processor secret key.
# =====================================================================
# Paths in THIS file must be ABSOLUTE (systemd does NOT expand %h inside an EnvironmentFile value; the CLI
# refuses a relative / %-bearing --spool). The unit ships a working %h-expanded DEFAULT spool.

# REQUIRED to run at all (the drain is DEFAULT-OFF and refuses without it). Also set it in
# ~/.config/vigil/alerts.env so `vigil alerts` watches this unit fail-closed from the start.
# VIGIL_BILLING_DRAIN_ENABLED=1

# REQUIRED: the Flutterwave webhook verif-hash secret (the SAME value the proxy's /webhooks/billing route uses).
# VIGIL_BILLING_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# REQUIRED: the processor secret key for the MANDATORY server-side transaction re-verify (without it the drain
# refuses — a verif-hash alone never grants value). Owner-provisioned; never paste it anywhere but this file.
# VIGIL_FLW_SECRET_KEY=

# OPTIONAL: the billing spool whose incoming/ is drained (default %h/.sigil/spool/billing). It MUST equal the
# proxy's VIGIL_BILLING_WEBHOOK_SPOOL (where /webhooks/billing writes), or nothing is ever drained.
# VIGIL_BILLING_SPOOL=/home/USER/.sigil/spool/billing
